{
  "hypothesis": "Optimize the sliding window technique for finding the maximum sum of an SxS submatrix by improving memory locality and loop order.",
  "transformations": [
    "Reorganized the loops to improve memory locality.",
    "Reduced the number of assertions for performance.",
    "Used a more efficient way to update the sum in the sliding window."
  ],
  "sources_kept": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "src/solution.cpp",
      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    std::vector<std::vector<int>> matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)\n        for(int j = 0; j < n; j++) \n            scanf(\"%d\", &(matrix[i][j]));\n\n    int sum = 0;\n    for(int i = 0; i < s; i++)\n        for(int j = 0; j < s; j++)\n            sum += matrix[i][j];\n\n    int mxSum = sum;\n\n    for(int i = 0; i <= n - s; i++) {\n        for(int j = 0; j <= n - s; j++) {\n            if (i == 0 && j == 0) continue;\n            if (i == 0) {\n                for(int k = 0; k < s; k++) {\n                    sum -= matrix[k][j - 1];\n                    sum += matrix[k][j + s - 1];\n                }\n            } else if (j == 0) {\n                for(int k = 0; k < s; k++) {\n                    sum -= matrix[i - 1][k];\n                    sum += matrix[i + s - 1][k];\n                }\n            } else {\n                for(int k = 0; k < s; k++) {\n                    sum -= matrix[i - 1][j + k - 1];\n                    sum -= matrix[i + s - 1][j + k - 1];\n                    sum += matrix[i + s - 1][j + k];\n                    sum += matrix[i - 1][j + k];\n                }\n            }\n            mxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\n        }\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", mxSum);\n}"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The code has been optimized to improve memory locality by processing rows and columns in a more sequential manner. The number of assertions has been reduced to enhance performance. The sliding window sum update has been streamlined for efficiency."
}
